## Line endings
##
## MTEX sources are LF. Without this, files committed from Windows arrive as
## CRLF and stay that way, which is how ~360 of them had drifted - a byte
## level edit then has to match \r\n or it silently fails to apply.
*.m text eol=lf

## Vendored code and test fixtures keep their bytes exactly as they are.
## Importers are parsed byte by byte and some fixtures carry deliberately
## odd line endings - see the lone CR that made .ang imports drop a row.
extern/** -text
data/** -text
